{
  "rationale": "The plant is split into a perception plant (sensors) and a motion plant (actuators). The specification automata bind sensor outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforce conservative obstacle recovery, and prevent unsafe or oscillatory behaviors. Helper states are used for recovery and last-resort full_rotate. The design maximizes forward/random_walk exploration when clear, and uses minimal, directed recovery when blocked.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensing and motion into distinct plants for clarity and modularity.",
    "Specification automata bind perception to action, enforce safe obstacle recovery, and prevent repeated or unsafe actions (e.g., no repeated full_rotate, no move_backward except in dedicated recovery)."
  ],
